{"hits": {"hits": [{"metadata": {"authors": [{"full_name": "Andrasi, A."}, {"full_name": "Day, M."}, {"full_name": "Doria, R."}, {"full_name": "Frenkel, J."}, {"full_name": "Taylor, J.C."}], "publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "182", "page_end": "124", "year": 1981, "page_start": "104", "journal_title": "Nucl.Phys.B"}], "texkeys": ["Andrasi:1980qw"], "imprints": [{"date": "1981"}], "abstracts": [{"value": "We demonstrate simply and directly that Bloch-Nordsieck inclusive cross sections are not in general infrared finite in non-abelian gauge theories treated by perturbation theory. We take the example q q \u2192\u03bb \u2217 + (gluons) to order \u03b1 s 2 , and use the Coulomb gauge in the lab frame, which greatly reduces the work. The relation to the Lee-Nauenberg theorem is discussed. In a very oversimplified model of bound quarks, the infrared divergence is replaced by a logarithm of the size of the bound state."}], "control_number": 9563, "dois": [{"value": "10.1016/0550-3213(81)90460-0"}], "titles": [{"title": "Soft Divergences in Perturbative {QCD}"}, {"title": "SOFT DIVERGENCES IN PERTURBATIVE QCD"}], "author_count": 5, "document_type": ["article"]}, "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/9563?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/9563?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/9563?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/9563?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/9563?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/9563?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A9563"}, "updated": "2023-03-07T02:29:08.549987+00:00", "created": "1980-07-01T00:00:00+00:00", "id": "9563"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Nucl.Phys.B%2C182%2C104&size=3&page=1&fields=control_number,titles.title,authors.full_name,author_count,